{
"opening": "The dateutil library is releasing version 0.13.2, which introduces several new features and bug fixes to its public API. The arrow project, which depends on dateutil, must upgrade to this release to ensure compatibility with the updated behavior of parsing, timezone handling, and recurrence rule generation.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m08",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the relativedelta class must maintain its documented tuple-based documentation structure without regression."
},
{
"id": "m12",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the parser.parse function must handle a tzinfos callable that explicitly returns None by not raising a ValueError."
},
{
"id": "m18",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the datetime_ambiguous, datetime_exists, resolve_imaginary, tzfile, tzrange, and tzstr symbols must be present and correctly documented for timezone awareness checks."
},
{
"id": "m25",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the timezone documentation must be restructured to improve clarity while maintaining all existing public functionality."
},
{
"id": "m27",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser.isoparse function must accept ISO 8601 time strings that use a comma as the decimal separator for fractional seconds."
},
{
"id": "m37",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser.isoparse function must interpret T24:00 as midnight on the following day, compliant with ISO 8601 standards."
},
{
"id": "m41",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the tzfile and tzoffset classes must support sub-minute time zone offsets when running on Python 3.6 or newer."
},
{
"id": "m43",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser.parse_isotime method must correctly handle time strings where the hour component is 24, representing midnight of the next day."
},
{
"id": "m53",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser.isoparse function must accept more than six fractional digits in the seconds portion of an ISO 8601 timestamp."
},
{
"id": "m58",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the tzfile implementation must correctly handle base offset changes during Daylight Saving Time transitions, specifically fixing issues related to Samoan time zone adjustments."
},
{
"id": "m66",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the isoparser.isoparse, parser.parse, and parserinfo classes must accept 'z' (lowercase z) as a valid representation for UTC time zone."
},
{
"id": "m68",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the cache_clear and set_cache_size functions must manage weak reference caching for tzoffset, tzstr, and gettz objects to improve performance and memory management."
},
{
"id": "m80",
"text": "In the dateutil library, the rrule and rruleset classes must support parsing EXDATE parameters within rrule strings to exclude specific dates from recurrence sets."
}
],
"closing": "Please ensure these changes are integrated into the dateutil codebase and verified against the arrow project's test suite before the release."
}
